codemap 9
tour feature-jump-to-definition
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Ctrl-click or double-click an identifier in any code view (document, source, peek, graph node) to go to its definition. The reader reaches for it to reach a definition without searching for it, as an editor with an LSP allows. A definition that is a symbol in the repo lands on that symbol: the matching step of the tour being read when there is one, otherwise the Source view. A definition inside a symbol (a field, a local) opens the Source view on its line. One outside the repo cannot be jumped to and is shown in the peek at the top of the References view instead, with a status line saying where it is; the References view is brought into sight for it, split off beside the centre view when no panel holds it. With a language server the answer arrives a few frames later, and until it does the status line says the word is being looked up; without one, the symbol of that name is used; prose files do nothing. No definition found is reported in the status bar.

